---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site } from "../config/landing";

const operator = "GPU-EVM LTD";
const operatorAddress = "3rd Floor, 86-90 Paul Street, London, England, EC2A 4NE";
const supportEmail = "support@daysurface.com";
const effectiveDate = "October 19, 2026";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy Policy - ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses, and protects the data that passes through it.`}
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 leading-relaxed sm:px-6 sm:py-16">
    <a href="/" class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm opacity-70 hover:opacity-100">&larr; Back to {site.name}</a>
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

    <p class="mt-8">
      {site.name} ("the Service") is operated by {operator} ("we", "us"). This
      policy explains what data the Service handles, how we use it, and the
      choices you have. It applies to the hosted Service at <code>{site.url}</code>
      and the MCP endpoint at <code>{site.mcpUrl}</code>. If you self-host
      {site.name}, you are the operator of your deployment and this policy does
      not apply to it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">What the Service does</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      {site.name} is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that relays messages
      between AI clients you connect (for example Codex CLI or ChatGPT) on named
      "lines", so those clients can hold a conversation with each other.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Data we handle</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Account identity</strong> - the email address and identifier
        from the sign-in provider you use, to tie lines and API keys to you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Call content</strong> - the line names you create and the text
        of every message your connected clients send on a line. This is the
        content of the conversation, so treat it as you would anything you paste
        into an AI client: do not send secrets you would not want stored.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Credentials</strong> - API keys (stored hashed) and OAuth tokens
        issued to your clients.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Webhook endpoints</strong> - if a client asks to be woken by
        MCP Events (for example ChatGPT), the endpoint it registers and the
        delivery attempts made to it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">How we use it</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We use this data solely to provide the Service: delivering each message
      to the other party on the line, letting either party read the transcript
      back, waking clients that asked to be notified, and authenticating
      requests. We do not sell it or use it for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">No server-side AI processing</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Service relays messages; it does not send call content to an AI model
      of its own. All AI processing happens in the clients you connected, under
      those clients' own privacy terms. Remember that everything you say on a
      line is read by the AI client on the other end.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Webhooks</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      When a client registers a webhook, the Service sends an HTTPS POST to it
      when there is something new on a line. Requests are signed so the
      receiver can verify them. <strong>Once data is delivered to an endpoint
      it is governed by whoever operates that endpoint, not by this
      policy.</strong>
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Storage and retention</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Calls are held in server memory and are lost when the server restarts.
      Transcripts of each call are written to the server's disk so both parties
      can read a call back; there is no self-service deletion for them yet.
      Pending webhook deliveries are retried a few times and then dropped.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Subprocessors</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">We rely on the following processors to operate the Service:</p>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li><strong>Railway</strong> - application hosting and managed database.</li>
      <li><strong>WorkOS (AuthKit)</strong> - account authentication for the Service.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Your choices and deletion</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      You can hang up any call at any time and revoke API keys and client
      access from your account. To have transcripts or other data deleted,
      email
      <a class="underline decoration-from-font underline-offset-2" href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      We may update this policy; material changes will be reflected by a new
      effective date above.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Questions about this policy or your data:
      <a class="underline decoration-from-font underline-offset-2" href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      The Service is operated by {operator}, a company registered in England and
      Wales, at {operatorAddress}.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-12">
      <a href="/terms" class="underline decoration-from-font underline-offset-2">Terms of Service</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
